#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SD0009 expect=violation domain=AE
#note "D-TA-8 flip (replaces FDA-SD0009-valid-aesod-AE.cdt, which pinned the AESOD-included behaviour): AESER=Y and only AESOD=Y. The FDA sheet enumerates seven criteria without AESOD, and the ruling drops the imported CDISC-CG0042 conjunct — AESOD records a circumstance of an already-serious event (AESOD=Y implies AESER=Y, not the reverse; a legacy criterion excluded from ICH E2A/E2B), so a serious event whose only raised flag is AESOD fires 'no criterion recorded'. Intended flip, not a regression."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 AESER=Y
dataset AE class=EVENTS label="Adverse Events"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col AESEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col AETERM   type=Char label="Reported Term for the Adverse Event"
col AESER    type=Char label="Serious Event"
col AESCAN   type=Char label="Involves Cancer"
col AESCONG  type=Char label="Congenital Anomaly or Birth Defect"
col AESDISAB type=Char label="Persist or Signif Disability/Incapacity"
col AESDTH   type=Char label="Results in Death"
col AESHOSP  type=Char label="Requires or Prolongs Hospitalization"
col AESLIFE  type=Char label="Is Life Threatening"
col AESOD    type=Char label="Occurred with Overdose"
col AESMIE   type=Char label="Other Medically Important Serious Event"
---
S1 | AE | 001 | 1 | OVERDOSE EVENT | Y | N | N | N | N | N | N | Y | N
S1 | AE | 001 | 2 | SEIZURE        | Y | N | N | N | N | Y | N | N | N
